<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Virga</title><link>https://virga.site</link><description>Virga is a Cloudflare-only baseline for launch directories, newsletters and portfolios — one owner, many readers, no console.</description><atom:link href="https://virga.site/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Shipping a launch directory on Cloudflare alone</title><link>https://virga.site/posts/shipping-a-directory</link><guid>https://virga.site/posts/shipping-a-directory</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>Upvotes, view counts and rankings without a database you have to run.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A launch directory needs exactly three things a static site cannot do:
count a view, take an upvote, and rank the list. Virga does all three in
one public Worker over D1, keyed on a daily visitor fingerprint that never
identifies a person.</p>
<pre><code class="language-ts">// one upvote per visitor per slug, per day
POST /v1/reactions/launches/acme { &quot;kind&quot;: &quot;upvote&quot; }
</code></pre>
<p>The ranking reads two small totals tables and never scans reactions.</p>
]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>Hello, world — why this site exists</title><link>https://virga.site/posts/hello-world</link><guid>https://virga.site/posts/hello-world</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>The first issue: what Virga is, and what you can expect in this inbox.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Welcome. This is the first issue of a newsletter that ships from a git
repository: every issue is a Markdown file, every send is a CLI command,
and the only thing running is a handful of Cloudflare Workers.</p>
<h2>What to expect</h2>
<ul>
<li>One email when something ships. Nothing else.</li>
<li>Every issue archived here, with a public view count.</li>
<li>Unsubscribe in one click, no questions.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Content is the configuration. The site renders the sections its folders
fill, so the same tree is a newsletter, a portfolio or a directory.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>See you in the next one.</p>
]]></content:encoded></item></channel></rss>